WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.691
A locale code names a language and,

2
00:00:03.691 --> 00:00:06.302
when it matters, its
script and region.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:11.318
So en-US is English
in the United States,

4
00:00:11.318 --> 00:00:15.473
and zh-Hant-TW is Traditional
Chinese in Taiwan.

5
00:00:15.873 --> 00:00:19.379
Most software uses BCP 47 tags,

6
00:00:19.379 --> 00:00:21.120
built from ISO codes.

7
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:26.062
General Translation uses BCP 47
codes for your source and target

8
00:00:26.062 --> 00:00:26.792
locales.

9
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.344
Set defaultLocale to your source,

10
00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:32.085
and list the targets in locales.

11
00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:36.444
The CLI checks every code before
it translates and stops on

12
00:00:36.444 --> 00:00:37.627
one that is not valid.

13
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.470
Your team now ships Brazilian
Portuguese with each release.
